  "short_bio": "Pakistani education activist and, at 17, the youngest Nobel Peace Prize laureate.",
  "biography": "Malala Yousafzai was born in Mingora, in Pakistan’s Swat Valley. When the Taliban restricted girls’ schooling she wrote a blog for the BBC under a pseudonym.\n\nOn 9 October 2012 a Taliban gunman shot her on her school bus. She was taken to Birmingham, England, for treatment. In 2013 she co-founded the Malala Fund and published I Am Malala.\n\nShe shared the 2014 Nobel Peace Prize with Kailash Satyarthi and graduated from Lady Margaret Hall, Oxford, in 2020.",
